2026-10-26T03:00:00Z  NOTE     Root cause, restated as measured: `~/Library/Caches/chadvis-projectm-qt/logs/chadvis-projectm-qt.log` logged `PresetScanner: Found 0 potential preset files` on every launch, because config had `preset_path = ''` and `file::presetsDir()` resolved to the empty `<dataDir>/presets`. projectM ships no preset pack, and its own test fixtures are not a product pack.
2026-10-26T02:52:00Z  DECISION Do not vendor the pack and do not build a runtime downloader. `cmake/PresetPack.cmake` fetches projectM-visualizer/presets-cream-of-the-crop (the pack the projectM project calls its default) into the BUILD directory, compiles its path in for a dev build, installs it to share/ and copies it into the .app. Licensing stays upstream's: LICENSE.md travels with the extracted tree and is installed beside it. Cost of the alternative: ~9,800 files in this repository, plus a ZIP reader Qt does not publicly ship.
2026-10-26T02:52:00Z  CHANGE   cmake/PresetPack.cmake (new), CMakeLists.txt (included after TargetSetup, which defines the targets it touches), src/util/FileUtils.cpp (presetsDir probes the bundled dir, the .app Resources dir, an app-relative share dir, honours CHADVIS_PRESET_DIR, and only prefers <dataDir>/presets when it actually holds a preset), src/qml_bridge/PresetBridge.{hpp,cpp} (folder property + setFolder: persists visualizer.preset_path and rescans), src/qml/panels/settings/VisualizerSettings.qml (Preset Library row: folder, Choose…, Rescan, count).
2026-10-26T03:00:18Z  EVIDENCE Real app run, 20 s, then SIGTERM. Log line 196: `PresetScanner: Scanning directory '/Users/derekvanee/Documents/chadvis-projectm-qt/build-fast/_deps/presets-cream-of-the-crop-master' (recursive=true)`. Line 200: `PresetScanner: Found 9795 potential preset files` at 03:00:22.156 — 3.6 s on the manager's scan worker, not the GUI thread.
2026-10-26T03:01:00Z  NOTE     projectM's own playlist walk is cheap by inspection: `Playlist::AddPath` (projectm-src/src/playlist/Playlist.cpp:83) walks recursively, compares `.milk` exactly, and appends filenames — no preset parsing at add time. So 9,795 files add in a directory walk, not a parse storm, and no startup regression is expected from the pack being found.
